  _globals['_IMAGESERVICE']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_IMAGESERVICE']._serialized_options = b'\222A\351\013\n\006Images\022\336\013Image API.\n\nUse this section to:\n- List OS/application images available within a scope\n- Retrieve image metadata (name, version, architecture, size)\n- Upload large image files using a server-mediated multipart upload flow\n\nResource model:\n- Images are scoped by a typed resource ID in the URL: `tenant.ULID` or `project.ULID`\n- Tenant-scoped images are visible to all projects under that tenant\n- Project-scoped images are visible only within that project (plus tenant images)\n- tenant_id is derived from the bearer token; clients do not pass tenant_id in requests\n- Storage internals (URL, checksum, bucket/object paths) are not exposed in API responses\n\nUpload flow (server-mediated multipart):\n1) StartImageUpload \342\200\224 declare the file (name, size, content type) and receive:\n   - upload_id (session identifier)\n   - part_size_bytes (use for every part except the last)\n   - max_in_flight_parts (recommended concurrency)\n2) Upload parts \342\200\224 upload each part by part_number:\n   - gRPC clients: Not supported for gRPC API, use REST API instead.\n   - REST clients: PUT /compute/images/{scope_id}/uploads/{upload_id}/parts/{part_number} with raw binary body\n3) GetImageUploadStatus \342\200\224 optional; returns uploaded parts to support resume/retry\n4) FinishImageUpload \342\200\224 validates contiguous parts (1..N) and total size; returns object_id\n5) AbortImageUpload \342\200\224 cancels an in-progress upload and frees server-side resources\n\nPagination:\n- List endpoints use cursor-based pagination (page_size + page_token)'
  _globals['_IMAGESERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListImages']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_IMAGESERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListImages']._serialized_options = b'\222A\250\002\n\006Images\022\032List images within a scope\032\271\001Lists images visible within the given scope. Pass a tenant resource ID (tenant.ULID) to list tenant-wide images, or a project resource ID (project.ULID) to list project + tenant images.J4\n\003200\022-\n\002OK\022\'\n%\032#.firebird.api.v1.ListImagesResponseb\020\n\016\n\nBearerAuth\022\000\202\323\344\223\002\034\022\032/compute/images/{scope_id}'
