  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE']._serialized_options = b'\222A\253\004\n\006Images\022\240\004Image upload API.\n\nServer-mediated multipart upload for large image files.\n\nStorage internals are never exposed. Clients interact only with `upload_id` and `object_id`.\n\nThe `scope_id` in the URL determines where the uploaded image will be stored:\n- `tenant.ULID` \342\200\224 tenant-scoped image (visible to all projects)\n- `project.ULID` \342\200\224 project-scoped image (visible only in that project)\n\n**For REST clients**, use `PUT /api/v1/compute/images/{scope_id}/uploads/{upload_id}/parts/{part_number}` with a raw binary body to upload individual parts.'
  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE'].methods_by_name['StartImageUpload']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE'].methods_by_name['StartImageUpload']._serialized_options = b'\222A\363\003\n\006Images\022 Start a new image upload session\032\346\002Declares a new large image file upload within the given scope. Returns an `upload_id` and the server-computed `part_size_bytes` to use for all parts except the last.\n\nThe scope_id determines image visibility after upload completes:\n- `tenant.ULID` \342\200\224 image visible to all projects under the tenant\n- `project.ULID` \342\200\224 image visible only within that project*\020StartImageUploadJ:\n\003200\0223\n\002OK\022-\n+\032).firebird.api.v1.StartImageUploadResponseb\020\n\016\n\nBearerAuth\022\000\202\323\344\223\002\'\"\"/compute/images/{scope_id}/uploads:\001*'
  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetImageUploadStatus']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_IMAGEUPLOADSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetImageUploadStatus']._serialized_options = b'\222A\203\003\n\006Images\022*Get image upload status and uploaded parts\032\344\001Returns the upload session state and the list of parts that have been successfully uploaded to storage.\n\nUse the returned part list to implement client-side resume: re-upload any missing parts before calling `FinishImageUpload`.*\024GetImageUploadStatusJ>\n\003200\0227\n\002OK\0221\n/\032-.firebird.api.v1.GetImageUploadStatusResponseb\020\n\016\n\nBearerAuth\022\000\202\323\344\223\002%\022#/compute/images/uploads/{upload_id}'
